LDAC is a high-definition Bluetooth audio codec developed by Sony to enhance sound quality through higher bitrates and reduced compression. It supports lossless or near-lossless audio streaming between devices and is supported by various earbud models such as the Nothing Ear (a), Nothing Ear Stick, and CMF Buds Pro 2, enabling high-quality music experiences.</data>
