<node id="Fast Charging">
  <data key="d0">Fast Charging</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Fast Charging is a feature that significantly enhances the usability and convenience of various devices such as CMF Buds Pro 2 and the Nothing Phone 1, among others. Specifically for the CMF Buds Pro 2, fast charging provides up to 4 hours of playback after just a 10-minute charge. When ANC (Active Noise Cancellation) is off, it can also offer up to 3 hours of listening time with another quick 10-minute charge. The feature allows users to enjoy longer use times between charges, making them more practical for daily activities.

For the Nothing Phone 1, fast charging enables swift recharging using compatible wired chargers, allowing this smartphone to charge quickly and efficiently. 

In general, fast charging benefits earbuds like those from Buds Pro by providing up to 2 hours of use after a mere 10-minute charge period or even longer depending on whether ANC is enabled. This ensures that users can enjoy extended listening sessions without being tethered to a power source for lengthy periods.

Moreover, fast charging in some instances might contribute more heat generation due to the rapid transfer of electrical energy. However, this trade-off between speed and efficiency does not seem to negatively impact other devices mentioned here like earbuds or phones that benefit from this feature.

Overall, fast charging is an advantageous technology designed to reduce downtime by providing swift charge times across a variety of gadgets including earbuds and smartphones, ensuring user convenience and extended usability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3b3089d626c59a7ef8835afdfb37254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8c347cbb4b796bbb29c806e9e99eddd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-761ab2f63c85934865840ccad2a1f48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd33025c132353d58f618d2df8ba210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ec2f81516f2860cb39745bfab9ea802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-439c5cf079599a3f3373b1059ecb4caf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93f6edcfacec45092a9cf547de8b797c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1751270700</data>
</node>
