6. "Google Fast Pair is a feature that enables quick and seamless pairing of devices with Android phones."
7. "Google Fast Pair is another quick pairing feature supported by the Buds Pro earbuds, designed for Android devices."

Looking at these, I notice that they all describe Google Fast Pair as a feature related to quick and seamless pairing. The slight differences are in what exactly it pairs with: some mention "Google devices," others say "Google-enabled devices," and several specify "Android phones" or specific products like CMF Buds Pro 2 or Buds Pro earbuds.

