<node id="AAC">
  <data key="d0">AAC</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AAC (Advanced Audio Coding) is a widely used audio codec supported by the Nothing Ear Stick earbuds.&lt;SEP&gt;AAC (Advanced Audio Coding) is another audio format supported by CMF Buds Pro 2 for high-quality audio transmission.&lt;SEP&gt;AAC is an audio coding standard used for lossy digital audio compression, commonly supported by iOS devices.&lt;SEP&gt;AAC is an audio format supported by the Buds for high-quality music playback.&lt;SEP&gt;An advanced audio codec supported by Nothing Ear (a) for high-quality sound transmission.</data>
