</node>
<node id="ANC">
  <data key="d0">ANC</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">ANC (Active Noise Cancellation) is not supported by Ear (open).&lt;SEP&gt;ANC stands for Active Noise Cancellation, a technology used by Nothing Ear (a) to enhance listening experience in noisy environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Noise Cancellation (ANC) is a feature in Ear (stick) that removes unwanted background noise during calls.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Noise Cancellation (ANC) is a feature of the Buds Pro earbuds that reduces background noise up to 45 dB at a bandwidth of 5000 Hz.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Noise Cancellation technology in Ear (a) provides up to 45 dB of noise reduction, enhancing audio clarity in noisy environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbe38a86de701a84c6998b00199044c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87ccc37a0e78b6e35c627713efb41b3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986d6ca4daaa54dfd11631f80f9fb5b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b3089d626c59a7ef8835afdfb37254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd33025c132353d58f618d2df8ba210</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1751270716</data>
</node>
<node id="ENC">
  <data key="d0">ENC</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">ENC (Environmental Noise Cancellation) is a feature of the Nothing Ear Stick earbuds that reduces background noise during calls.&lt;SEP&gt;ENC stands for Environmental Noise Cancellation, a feature of Nothing Ear (a) that improves call quality by reducing background noise.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Noise Cancellation (ENC) ensures others don't hear background noise when speaking through the microphone.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Noise Cancellation (ENC) is a feature designed to remove unwanted background noise during calls, ensuring clear communication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbe38a86de701a84c6998b00199044c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e527ebc82d3e91d040743f1b3884d81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986d6ca4daaa54dfd11631f80f9fb5b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b3089d626c59a7ef8835afdfb37254</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1751270716</data>
</node>
<node id="IP54 Rating">
  <data key="d0">IP54 Rating</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A rating indicating resistance to water and dust as per IEC standard 60529.&lt;SEP&gt;Ear (a) is rated IP54 for water and dust resistance, providing protection against splashes and particles but not immersion in liquids.&lt;SEP&gt;The IP54 rating indicates that the Buds Pro earbuds are dustproof (class 5) and splashproof (class 4), based on IEC 60529 standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The IP54 rating indicates that the CMF Buds are dustproof and waterproof up to a certain level, based on the IEC 60529 standard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-458fb6678632e1a5048fc67fa95a614a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87ccc37a0e78b6e35c627713efb41b3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1843631bbc6580a0ba48e4e755c7d90a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b3089d626c59a7ef8835afdfb37254</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1751270716</data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Capacity">
  <data key="d0">Battery Capacity</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The concept of Battery Capacity pertains to the energy-storing capacity of electronic devices such as earbuds or phones. This measure is expressed in units of milliampere-hours (mAh) and acts as a critical determinant for overall performance.

Specifically regarding earbuds, one model features a battery with a capacity of 5000 mAh, which provides extended usage time. This indicates that the earbuds have an impressive ability to hold charge over prolonged periods when in use. Another model showcases an Ear (open) configuration equipped with two earbuds each holding 64 mAh and an additional charging case capable of 635 mAh capacity.

In a different context, the Buds Pro earbuds exhibit a battery capacity of 55mAh per earbud and 460mAh for their respective charging case. This also supports extended usage time under various conditions, aligning with the first statement's assertion about a high-capacity battery providing long usage periods.

Incorporating another entity named 'The Phone', it has a battery capacity of 5000 mAh. The charging process for this phone utilizes PPS (Power Path Sharing) protocol charger and can be fully charged in around one hour under optimal conditions, suggesting rapid recharging capabilities despite its relatively large battery size.

In summary, the battery capacity across these entities ranges from an impressive 5000 mAh to a more modest figure like the Ear's components with capacities of 64mAh and 635mAh for each earbud and charging case respectively. The Buds Pro model adds another dimension with its specific specifications. The Phone showcases a large capacity battery that can be rapidly charged using PPS protocol under ideal conditions, underscoring efficiency in power management across various devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1843631bbc6580a0ba48e4e755c7d90a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-335683f97c8848d2aafed7c27907ddaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-506079618b7f18b62044e8932e5a2f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b3089d626c59a7ef8835afdfb37254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8c347cbb4b796bbb29c806e9e99eddd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd33025c132353d58f618d2df8ba210</data>
