<node id="Neckband Pro">
  <data key="d0">Neckband Pro</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Neckband Pro is a high-tech audio device that was originally produced by Sony but is currently manufactured by Samsung instead of being developed by Nothing as previously mentioned. This device has evolved with several advanced features such as ANC (Active Noise Cancellation) technology, allowing users to enjoy immersive listening experiences without external disturbances. The customizable EQ settings provide personalized audio tuning options for different music genres and preferences.

The Neckband Pro offers a notable battery performance, boasting long-lasting power in both music playback and call handling modes. Despite not supporting wireless charging directly, it can be efficiently charged using a Type-C cable via the provided connection port. An innovative aspect of this device is its dual connectivity feature; it enables seamless connection to two mobile devices simultaneously, providing flexibility for users who often switch between various audio sources.

Furthermore, the Neckband Pro comes equipped with fast charging capabilities, ensuring that users can quickly restore battery life without needing a prolonged charge period. These features collectively make the Neckband Pro an attractive option for audiophiles and tech enthusiasts seeking a device that combines advanced technology, convenience, and reliability in audio playback and connectivity options.

In summary, the Neckband Pro is an audio-centric product developed by Nothing and currently manufactured by Sony. It integrates ANC capabilities, customizable EQ settings, long battery life, fast charging support, and dual connectivity for an exceptional listening experience across multiple devices.</data>
