<node id="Power Adaptor">
  <data key="d0">Power Adaptor</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Power Adaptor is a device used for charging electronic devices and converts AC to DC power.&lt;SEP&gt;The power adaptor is an electronic device used to charge various devices, converting AC to DC current and ensuring safe charging operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8ca79f85802bd5627b38a61937dc097&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0973d7d7882ae44716cb572ca4b5ffab</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1751270768</data>
</node>
<node id="USB Cable">
  <data key="d0">USB Cable</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A USB cable is a component used to connect the power adaptor to a device for charging purposes. It must be properly connected and in good condition to ensure effective charging.&lt;SEP&gt;USB Cable is used to connect the power adaptor to electronic devices for charging purposes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8ca79f85802bd5627b38a61937dc097&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0973d7d7882ae44716cb572ca4b5ffab</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1751270768</data>
</node>
<node id="Charging Port">
  <data key="d0">Charging Port</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The charging port is an interface on a device where the USB cable connects to enable charging. It may become dirty or damaged, affecting the charging process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8ca79f85802bd5627b38a61937dc097</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1751270768</data>
</node>
